// 31575
[struct_31575]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,The Death interface displays items which are held by Death, which you may reclaim.

// 31576
[struct_31576]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,The 'protected items' section displays items which cost you nothing to save. Your most expensive items are listed here by default.<br><br>By default 3 items are protected and this can be increased with effects from certain prayers or items.

// 31577
[struct_31577]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,The 'saved items' section displays items which will be returned to you, but you will have to pay to get them back.<br><br>Hover your mouse over an item to see how much it costs to save.<br><br>The total value of all saved items is listed at the bottom of the interface.

// 31578
[struct_31578]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,The 'lost items' section displays items which you choose not to save or protect. These items will make it cheaper to reclaim other items you choose to save.<br><br>If you are viewing the interface via the 'Deathkeep' button, this area will also display items which are always lost on death and items carried by your Beast of Burden.<br><br>The sacrificed item value is the total cost reduction these items offer.

// 31579
[struct_31579]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,This 'always saved' section displays items which are protected on death. These items will be returned once you decide which items to keep or lose and pay any costs.

// 31580
[struct_31580]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,You can drag items between each section, excluding 'always saved' or use right click options to select what to do with an item.

// 31581
[struct_31581]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,Once you have decided on what to save and what to sacrifice, select the confirm button.<br><br>This will open a panel summarising what will happen and you will then be able to pay any costs that are required.

// 31582
[struct_31582]
param=param_3824,Death
param=param_3827,If you don't have enough gold, you may close the interface and return at a later date. You have a full 24 hours of gameplay before you will be unable to reclaim your items.

